{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "def is_not_prime(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies if a given integer is a non-prime number.\n    Returns True for non-prime numbers, False for prime numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 1:\n        return True  # Numbers less than or equal to 1 are not prime\n    if number == 2:\n        return False # 2 is prime\n    if number % 2 == 0:\n        return True  # Even numbers greater than 2 are not prime\n\n    # Check for odd divisors from 3 up to the square root of the number\n    # If a divisor is found, the number is not prime\n    for i in range(3, int(number**0.5) + 1, 2):\n        if number % i == 0:\n            return True\n\n    return False # No divisors found, so the number is prime"}
