{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\n    P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n-P(n-1)) for n > 2, with P(1)=1 and P(2)=1.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = [0] * (n + 1)\n\n    if n == 1 or n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    memo[1] = 1\n    memo[2] = 1\n\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        # Calculate P(i) using previously computed values.\n        # P(i-1) and i - P(i-1) are guaranteed to be valid indices >= 1 for Newman-Conway sequence.\n        memo[i] = memo[memo[i - 1]] + memo[i - memo[i - 1]]\n\n    return memo[n]"}
