{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def _rotate_left(binary_str: str, positions: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a binary string to the left by a given number of positions.\"\"\"\n    n = len(binary_str)\n    if n == 0:\n        return \"\"\n    # Ensure positions is within the string length for unique rotations\n    actual_positions = positions % n\n    return binary_str[actual_positions:] + binary_str[:actual_positions]\n\ndef _binary_to_decimal(binary_str: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Converts a binary string to its decimal integer equivalent.\"\"\"\n    if not binary_str:\n        return 0\n    return int(binary_str, 2)\n\ndef _is_odd(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if an integer is an odd number.\"\"\"\n    return number % 2 != 0\n\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, rotation_count: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the number of numbers with an odd value when rotating a binary string \n    the given number of times.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    \n    # Iterate 'rotation_count' times, considering each 'i' as the number of left shifts\n    for i in range(rotation_count):\n        rotated_str = _rotate_left(binary_string, i)\n        decimal_val = _binary_to_decimal(rotated_str)\n        if _is_odd(decimal_val):\n            odd_count += 1\n            \n    return odd_count"}
