{"task_id": "Mbpp/116", "solution": "def tuple_to_int(input_tuple: tuple) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a tuple of positive integers into a single integer by concatenating their digits.\n    An empty tuple returns 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_tuple:\n        return 0\n\n    # Convert each integer in the tuple to its string representation\n    string_elements = [str(num) for num in input_tuple]\n\n    # Join the string representations to form a single string\n    concatenated_string = \"\".join(string_elements)\n\n    # Convert the concatenated string to an integer and return\n    return int(concatenated_string)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/119", "solution": "def search(array: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the element that appears only once in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Assumes all other elements appear in pairs.\n    \"\"\"\n    left, right = 0, len(array) - 1\n\n    while left <= right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n\n        # If mid is the last element or the current element is different from the next\n        # AND (mid is the first element or the current element is different from the previous)\n        # then this is the unique element.\n        # This condition handles cases where the unique element is at the start, end, or middle\n        if (mid == len(array) - 1 or array[mid] != array[mid + 1]) and \\\n           (mid == 0 or array[mid] != array[mid - 1]):\n            return array[mid]\n\n        # Determine which side of 'mid' to search\n        # If mid is even, check if array[mid] == array[mid+1]\n        # If mid is odd, check if array[mid] == array[mid-1]\n        if mid % 2 == 0:  # mid is at an even index\n            if mid + 1 < len(array) and array[mid] == array[mid + 1]:\n                left = mid + 2  # The pair is on the left, unique must be on the right\n            else:\n                right = mid     # The unique element is either array[mid] or on the left\n        else:  # mid is at an odd index\n            if array[mid] == array[mid - 1]:\n                left = mid + 1  # The pair is on the left, unique must be on the right\n            else:\n                right = mid - 1 # The unique element is either array[mid-1] or on the left (but mid-1 is even)"}
