{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number can be represented as a sum of distinct non-zero powers of 2.\n    This is true if the number is positive and even.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 0:\n        return False\n    # A number can be represented as a sum of non-zero powers of 2\n    # if and only if its binary representation does not include 2^0 (which is 1).\n    # This means the number must be even.\n    return number % 2 == 0"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def count_zeros(array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of zero values in the array.\"\"\"\n    zero_count = 0\n    for x in array:\n        if x == 0:\n            zero_count += 1\n    return zero_count\n\ndef count_non_zeros(array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of non-zero values in the array.\"\"\"\n    non_zero_count = 0\n    for x in array:\n        if x != 0:\n            non_zero_count += 1\n    return non_zero_count\n\ndef calculate_ratio(zero_count: int, non_zero_count: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the mathematical ratio of zeros to non-zeros.\"\"\"\n    return float(zero_count) / non_zero_count\n\ndef zero_count(array: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the ratio of zeroes to non-zeroes in an array of integers.\n    Orchestrates counting and ratio calculation using helper functions.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_zeros = count_zeros(array)\n    num_non_zeros = count_non_zeros(array)\n    return calculate_ratio(num_zeros, num_non_zeros)"}
