{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(array, n, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given element is a majority element in the sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Binary search to find the first occurrence of the element\n    first_occurrence = -1\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            first_occurrence = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    if first_occurrence == -1:\n        return False\n\n    # Binary search to find the last occurrence of the element\n    last_occurrence = -1\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            last_occurrence = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    count = last_occurrence - first_occurrence + 1\n    return count > n // 2"}
