{"task_id": "Mbpp/232", "solution": "def _validate_inputs(input_list: list, n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    This helper conceptually validates inputs.\n    Per constraints, explicit isinstance checks are not performed here;\n    it assumes correct types and allows Python's natural error handling for mismatches.\n    \"\"\"\n    return True\n\ndef _handle_edge_cases(input_list: list, n: int) -> tuple[bool, list]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Handles specific edge cases for n, such as n being non-positive or exceeding list length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return (True, [])\n    if n >= len(input_list):\n        return (True, sorted(input_list, reverse=True))\n    return (False, [])\n\ndef _get_n_largest(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts the list in descending order and extracts the top n items.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_list = sorted(input_list, reverse=True)\n    return sorted_list[:n]\n\ndef larg_nnum(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a list containing the n largest items from the input list in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_inputs(input_list, n)\n\n    should_return_early, result = _handle_edge_cases(input_list, n)\n    if should_return_early:\n        return result\n\n    return _get_n_largest(input_list, n)"}
