{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-positioned bits (0, 2, 4, etc.) of a given number to 1.\n    Odd-positioned bits remain unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Determine the effective bit length of the number.\n    # For 0, bit_length() is 0, but we need to consider at least bit 0 for setting.\n    effective_bit_length = number.bit_length()\n    if number == 0:\n        effective_bit_length = 1\n\n    # Generate a mask with 1s at all even bit positions up to the effective_bit_length.\n    even_mask = 0\n    # Iterate through even bit positions: 0, 2, 4, ...\n    # The loop upper bound ensures all relevant even bits within the number's length are covered.\n    for i in range(0, effective_bit_length, 2):\n        even_mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    # Perform a bitwise OR operation to set the even bits.\n    return number | even_mask"}
