{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    This is equivalent to finding the Longest Common Subsequence (LCS)\n    between the input string and its reverse.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    rs = s[::-1]  # The reverse of the input string\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the LCS of s[0...i-1] and rs[0...j-1]\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Fill the dp table using bottom-up approach\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, n + 1):\n            if s[i - 1] == rs[j - 1]:\n                # If characters match, extend the LCS\n                dp[i][j] = 1 + dp[i - 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                # If characters don't match, take the maximum from\n                # excluding a character from s or from rs\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i - 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    # The length of the LPS of s is the LCS of s and rs\n    return dp[n][n]"}
