{"task_id": "Mbpp/261", "solution": "def division_elements(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise division between two tuples of equal length.\n    Returns a tuple containing integer results of the division.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _validate_inputs(t1: tuple, t2: tuple) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if two tuples have the same length.\"\"\"\n        return len(t1) == len(t2)\n\n    def _perform_division(t1: tuple, t2: tuple) -> tuple:\n        \"\"\"Divides elements of t1 by elements of t2, returning a tuple of integer results.\"\"\"\n        results = [int(a / b) for a, b in zip(t1, t2)]\n        return tuple(results)\n\n    # As per design, input validation is performed.\n    # Constraints imply no explicit error handling for invalid lengths in this context.\n    _validate_inputs(tuple1, tuple2)\n    \n    return _perform_division(tuple1, tuple2)"}
