{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "def max_aggregate(tuple_list: list) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum aggregate value from a list of (identifier, value) tuples.\n    Aggregates values for each identifier and returns the identifier with the highest total sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    aggregated_data = {}\n    for identifier, value in tuple_list:\n        aggregated_data[identifier] = aggregated_data.get(identifier, 0) + value\n\n    if not aggregated_data:\n        # Handle case of empty input list (or list with no numeric values)\n        # Returning (None, 0) or similar default might be appropriate based on specific requirements,\n        # but for this problem, an empty list implies no aggregate, so (None, 0) is a safe default.\n        return (None, 0) \n        \n    # Find the key-value pair with the maximum value\n    max_identifier, max_value = max(aggregated_data.items(), key=lambda item: item[1])\n\n    return (max_identifier, max_value)"}
