{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Set the leftmost unset bit in the given integer.\n    This function finds the most significant 0-bit and changes it to 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    bit_length = number.bit_length()\n\n    # Iterate from the most significant bit down to 0 to find the leftmost unset bit.\n    for k in range(bit_length - 1, -1, -1):\n        if (number & (1 << k)) == 0:\n            return number | (1 << k)\n    \n    # If all bits within bit_length are set (e.g., number is 2^n - 1),\n    # the leftmost unset bit is at position bit_length.\n    return number | (1 << bit_length)"}
