{"task_id": "Mbpp/395", "solution": "def _count_characters(input_string: str) -> dict[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"Counts the occurrences of each character in the input string.\n    Returns a dictionary mapping each character to its frequency.\"\"\"\n    char_counts = {}\n    for char in input_string:\n        char_counts[char] = char_counts.get(char, 0) + 1\n    return char_counts\n\ndef _find_first_unique(input_string: str, char_counts: dict[str, int]) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Finds the first character in the input string that has a count of 1.\n    Iterates through the string to maintain order of appearance.\"\"\"\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char_counts[char] == 1:\n            return char\n    return None\n\ndef first_non_repeating_character(input_string: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Finds the first non-repeated character in a given string.\n    Returns None if all characters are repeated or the string is empty.\"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return None\n\n    char_counts = _count_characters(input_string)\n    return _find_first_unique(input_string, char_counts)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "def get_max_sum(n, memo={}):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum for n using the recursive equation f(n) = max((f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    Uses memoization to optimize performance by storing previously computed results.\"\"\"\n    if n in memo:\n        return memo[n]\n\n    if n <= 0:\n        return n\n\n    sum_of_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2, memo) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3, memo) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4, memo) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5, memo)\n    )\n\n    result = max(sum_of_parts, n)\n    memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
