{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(array: list) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair of numbers with the highest product from a given array of integers.\n    Assumes the input array contains at least two integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n    \n    # Initialize max_prod with the product of the first valid pair.\n    # This handles cases where all products might be negative.\n    max_prod = array[0] * array[1]\n    result_pair = (array[0], array[1])\n\n    # Iterate through all unique pairs of numbers in the array.\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            current_num1 = array[i]\n            current_num2 = array[j]\n            current_product = current_num1 * current_num2\n\n            # If the current pair's product is greater, update the max product and the result pair.\n            if current_product > max_prod:\n                max_prod = current_product\n                result_pair = (current_num1, current_num2)\n\n    return result_pair"}
