{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list using the shell sort algorithm with Knuth gap sequence.\n    Returns a new sorted list without modifying the original.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original list\n    arr_copy = arr[:]\n\n    # Helper to generate Knuth sequence gaps\n    def _generate_gap_sequence(size: int) -> list:\n        gaps = []\n        k = 1\n        while True:\n            gap = (3**k - 1) // 2\n            if gap > size // 3:  # Knuth's suggestion, or simply gap >= size depending on variant\n                break\n            gaps.append(gap)\n            k += 1\n        return gaps[::-1] if gaps else [1] # Return in descending order, ensure at least [1] for tiny arrays\n\n    # Helper for gap-based insertion sort\n    def _insertion_sort_with_gap(current_arr: list, gap: int) -> None:\n        for i in range(gap, len(current_arr)):\n            temp = current_arr[i]\n            j = i\n            while j >= gap and current_arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                current_arr[j] = current_arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            current_arr[j] = temp\n\n    gaps = _generate_gap_sequence(n)\n\n    for gap in gaps:\n        _insertion_sort_with_gap(arr_copy, gap)\n\n    return arr_copy"}
