{"task_id": "Mbpp/564", "solution": "def count_Pairs(lst: list[int], length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of possible unordered pairs where both elements are unequal.\n    The length parameter is ignored as the function operates on the list itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    n = len(lst)\n\n    # Iterate through all unique pairs (i, j) where i < j\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            # Check if the elements in the pair are unequal\n            if lst[i] != lst[j]:\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
