{"task_id": "Mbpp/572", "solution": "def two_unique_nums(numbers: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes duplicate numbers from a list, returning only those that appear exactly once.\n    The original order of the unique numbers is preserved.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n    for num in numbers:\n        counts[num] = counts.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    result = []\n    for num in numbers:\n        if counts[num] == 1:\n            result.append(num)\n            \n    return result"}
