{"task_id": "Mbpp/607", "solution": "import re\n\ndef find_literals(text: str, pattern: str) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Searches a string for the first occurrence of a regex pattern and returns the match and its indices.\n    Returns (None, -1, -1) if no match is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    compiled_pattern = re.compile(pattern)\n    match = compiled_pattern.search(text)\n\n    if match:\n        return (match.group(0), match.start(), match.end())\n    else:\n        return (None, -1, -1)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "def bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculate the nth Bell number using the Bell triangle method.\n    The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row (0-indexed) of the Bell triangle.\"\"\"\n\n    # Nested helper function to build the Bell triangle up to row k.\n    def _calculate_bell_triangle(k: int) -> list[list[int]]:\n        \"\"\"Calculates Bell triangle up to row k.\n        Returns a list of lists representing the triangle.\"\"\"\n        if k == 0:\n            return [[1]] # Base case: B_0.\n\n        triangle = [[1]] # Initialize with the row for B_0.\n        for i in range(1, k + 1):\n            prev_row = triangle[i - 1]\n            current_row = [prev_row[-1]] # First element of the current row is the last of the previous row.\n            for j in range(len(prev_row)):\n                current_row.append(current_row[-1] + prev_row[j]) # Subsequent elements are sum of left and top-left.\n            triangle.append(current_row)\n        return triangle\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 # B_0 is defined as 1.\n\n    # Build the complete Bell triangle up to the nth row.\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row (0-indexed).\n    full_triangle = _calculate_bell_triangle(n)\n    return full_triangle[n][0]"}
