{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list, list2: list, size: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    Uses a binary search approach to find the two middle elements without merging the lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _find_kth_element(arr1, arr2, k):\n        # Ensure arr1 is the shorter or equal length list for simpler partitioning logic.\n        # This swap helps optimize the recursion depth and simplifies index calculations.\n        if len(arr1) > len(arr2):\n            return _find_kth_element(arr2, arr1, k)\n\n        # Base cases\n        # If arr1 is empty, the kth element must be in arr2.\n        if not arr1:\n            return arr2[k - 1]\n        # If we need the 1st element, it's the minimum of the first elements of both arrays.\n        if k == 1:\n            return min(arr1[0], arr2[0])\n\n        # Determine how many elements to take from arr1 and arr2.\n        # Try to take k/2 elements from arr1, but not more than arr1 has.\n        idx1 = min(k // 2, len(arr1))\n        # Take the remaining elements from arr2 to reach k.\n        idx2 = k - idx1\n\n        # Compare elements at the partitioning points.\n        if arr1[idx1 - 1] < arr2[idx2 - 1]:\n            # Discard arr1[:idx1] and recursively search in the remaining parts.\n            # We need to find the (k - idx1)-th element in the combined remainder.\n            return _find_kth_element(arr1[idx1:], arr2, k - idx1)\n        elif arr1[idx1 - 1] > arr2[idx2 - 1]:\n            # Discard arr2[:idx2] and recursively search in the remaining parts.\n            # We need to find the (k - idx2)-th element in the combined remainder.\n            return _find_kth_element(arr1, arr2[idx2:], k - idx2)\n        else:\n            # If elements are equal, this element is the k-th smallest.\n            return arr1[idx1 - 1] # Can be arr2[idx2 - 1] as well\n\n    # For two lists of size 'size', the total number of elements is 2 * size.\n    # Since the total number of elements is always even, the median is the average of\n    # the (size)-th and (size + 1)-th smallest elements in the merged array.\n    \n    # We use the _find_kth_element helper function which is 1-indexed for 'k'.\n    median_val1 = _find_kth_element(list1, list2, size)\n    median_val2 = _find_kth_element(list1, list2, size + 1)\n\n    return (median_val1 + median_val2) / 2.0"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/629", "solution": "def Split(numbers: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filter even numbers from input list.\n\n    Args:\n        numbers (list): List of numbers to filter\n\n    Returns:\n        list: List containing only even numbers from input\n    \"\"\"\n    return [num for num in numbers if num % 2 == 0]"}
