{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit number to the left by 'd' positions.\n    Bits shifted out from the left wrap around to the right side.\n    \"\"\"\n    BIT_COUNT = 32\n    BIT_MASK = 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n    # Normalize the rotation count to be within 0 and BIT_COUNT-1.\n    d_normalized = d % BIT_COUNT\n\n    # Extract the bits that will be shifted out from the left and wrap around to the right.\n    wrap_bits = number >> (BIT_COUNT - d_normalized)\n\n    # Perform the left shift, ensuring the result is capped at 32 bits.\n    shifted_number = (number << d_normalized) & BIT_MASK\n\n    # Combine the left-shifted part with the wrapped-around bits.\n    result = shifted_number | wrap_bits\n\n    return result"}
