{"task_id": "Mbpp/803", "solution": "def is_perfect_square(number: float) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given number is a perfect square.\n    It returns True for perfect squares and False otherwise, including for negative inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _validate_input(n):\n        # Returns False if the number is negative, as perfect squares must be non-negative.\n        return n >= 0\n\n    def _calculate_integer_square_root(n):\n        \"\"\"Calculates the integer square root of a non-negative number using binary search.\"\"\"\n        if n == 0:\n            return 0\n        \n        low = 1\n        high = int(n)\n        ans = 0\n\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = (low + high) // 2\n            if mid * mid == n:\n                return mid\n            elif mid * mid < n:\n                ans = mid\n                low = mid + 1\n            else: # mid * mid > n\n                high = mid - 1\n        return ans\n\n    if not _validate_input(number):\n        return False\n\n    sqrt_int = _calculate_integer_square_root(number)\n    # Compare the square of the integer root with the original number.\n    # Convert to float for robust comparison if the original number was a float.\n    return float(sqrt_int * sqrt_int) == number"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/804", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef is_product_even(numbers: List[int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Check whether the product of numbers in a list is even.\n\n    Args:\n        numbers: List of integers\n\n    Returns:\n        bool: True if product is even, False if odd\n    \"\"\"\n    # The product is even if any number in the list is zero or even.\n    # Otherwise, if all numbers are odd (or the list is empty), the product is odd.\n    for number in numbers:\n        if number == 0 or number % 2 == 0:\n            return True\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/806", "solution": "```python\ndef max_run_uppercase(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the maximum run of consecutive uppercase characters in a string.\n\n    Args:\n        input_string (str): The input string to analyze\n\n    Returns:\n        int: Length of the longest consecutive uppercase character sequence\n    \"\"\"\n    max_run = 0\n    current_run = 0\n    for char in input_string:\n        if 'A' <= char <= 'Z':  # Check if character is an uppercase letter\n            current_run += 1\n            if current_run > max_run:\n                max_run = current_run\n        else:\n            current_run = 0\n    return max_run\n```"}
